WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
Now let's talk about burn injuries.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.960
Burns can happen in an instant, whether from the sun,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.800
hot liquids, electricity, or chemicals.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.640
Before we look at the degrees, remember that any burn

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.600
on the face, hands, feet, or genitals,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.080
or any burn larger than two to three inches

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.200
needs to be evaluated

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.400
by a healthcare professional immediately.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:21.240
If someone's clothing is on fire,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.059
have them stop, drop, and roll immediately,

00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:27.040
and use a blanket or water to smother the flames.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.040
Once the fire is out, call 911.

00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:33.720
We categorize burns by how deep the damage goes.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.200
First-degree burns.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.240
These are superficial, like a typical sunburn.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.439
The skin is red, painful, and swollen.

00:00:41.439 --> 00:00:44.520
To treat this, rinse the area with cool running water

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.439
for 10 to 20 minutes until the pain subsides,

00:00:47.439 --> 00:00:50.279
then cover it with a non-stick dressing.

00:00:50.279 --> 00:00:51.959
Second-degree burns.

00:00:51.959 --> 00:00:54.240
These go deeper and are very painful,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.520
often appearing blotchy with blisters.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:57.959
Treatment is the same.

00:00:57.959 --> 00:01:01.439
Cool water for 10 to 20 minutes and a non-stick dressing,

00:01:01.439 --> 00:01:04.400
but it is vital that you do not pop the blisters

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:07.139
as they protect the skin while it heals.

00:01:07.139 --> 00:01:08.959
Third-degree burns.

00:01:08.959 --> 00:01:11.239
These are severe, full-thickness burns

00:01:11.239 --> 00:01:14.599
where the skin may look charred, white, or leathery,

00:01:14.599 --> 00:01:17.080
potentially exposing fat or muscle.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.599
Paradoxically, these may be less painful

00:01:19.599 --> 00:01:21.519
if the nerves have been damaged.

00:01:21.519 --> 00:01:23.559
When providing care for severe burns,

00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:26.440
do not remove any clothing that is stuck to the skin,

00:01:27.279 --> 00:01:29.239
though you should gently remove jewelry or loose clothing

00:01:29.239 --> 00:01:31.559
before swelling makes it difficult.

00:01:31.559 --> 00:01:34.080
Cover the area with a clean, dry dressing

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.860
and keep the person warm to prevent shock.

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:39.959
Most importantly, never apply butter, ointments,

00:01:39.959 --> 00:01:42.199
or home remedies to a severe burn

00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:44.760
and do not immerse large burns in water

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.120
as this can interfere with medical treatment.

